    },
    {
      "family": "aggressive detour, minimal stop (turn 10)",
      "turns": "10",
      "result": "7/9 passes, avg ≈ 66 s, 2 collisions"
    },
    {
      "family": "danger‑close + existing stop/detour (turn 11)",
      "turns": "11",
      "result": "7/9 passes, avg ≈ 80 s, 1 collision, 1 time‑limit"
    }
  ],
  "candidates": [
    {
      "idea": "Add side/back mover detection and trigger immediate in‑place rotation (detour) instead of _evade which may still move forward",
      "new_family": true,
      "for": "충돌이 뒤쪽·측면에서 발생하는 경우를 빠르게 회피",
      "risk": "불필요한 회전이 늘어나 평균 시간 증가"
    },
    {
      "idea": "Increase forward speed scaling factor (allow v up to 1.5 m/s when gap ≥ 2.5 m) to reduce total travel time",
      "new_family": true,
      "for": "전체 실행 시간 평균 60 s 이하 달성",
      "risk": "고속 전진 시 센서‑기반 충돌 회피가 늦어져 새로운 충돌 위험"
    },
    {
      "idea": "Expand _danger_close to use robot body rear offset (‑0.70 m) so rear movers are detected earlier and treated with larger safety margin",
      "new_family": false,
      "for": "뒤쪽 물체에 대한 거리 판단 오류 보정",
      "risk": "과도한 정지·우회로 인해 시간 초과 가능"
    }
  ],
  "chosen": "side/back detection with immediate rotation (candidate 1) because it directly fixes the early collision that the current _evade does not handle.",
  "target": "controller logic and new helper _danger_side",
  "direction": "1. Define _DANGER_SIDE_ANGLE = math.radians(45) and a function _danger_side(pose,movers) that returns +1 or -1 depending on whether a mover within _DANGER_DIST lies on the left or right side (|bearing|>_DANGER_SIDE_ANGLE). 2. In controller(), after obtaining movers, call side_dir = _danger_side(pose,movers). 3. If side_dir is not None, set c.state='detour', c.detour_w = 0.5*side_dir, c.detour_t=t and immediately return (0.0, c.detour_w, False). 4. Keep existing front‑gap stop/detour logic for frontal obstacles. 5. Ensure _detour_side() is still used for normal detour but is bypassed when side_dir triggers. 6. No other constants are changed.",
